=== Diagnostic Steps ===
----

# Confirm the Drift
#* Connect the controller to a PS5 or PC.
#* Leave the analog stick untouched.
#* You can use a controller testing software on PC:  https://ds.daidr.me/
#* Observe:
#** Character or cursor movement
#** Axis movement in controller test software
# Rule Out Software Causes
#* Reset the controller using the rear reset pin (5–10 seconds).
#* Update controller firmware on PS5.
#* Re-test for drift.
#* If drift persists → hardware fault confirmed.
# Check Drift Severity
#* Slight, inconsistent drift → likely contamination.
#* Strong, constant drift in one direction → worn potentiometer.
#* Drift on both axes → joystick module failure.
# Inspect for Physical Wear
#* Rotate and press the stick.
#* Note:
#** Loose feel
#** Grinding or resistance
#** Stick not returning to center
# Decide Repair Path
#* Minor drift → cleaning attempt.
#* Persistent drift → joystick module replacement.

----

=== Repair Steps ===

==== Repair Option 1: Cleaning (Temporary / Minor Drift) ====

# Power off and disconnect the controller.
# Remove faceplate and access the analog stick.
# Blow compressed air around the base of the stick.
# Apply 90%+ isopropyl alcohol or contact cleaner to the stick base.
# Rotate the stick fully in all directions for 20–30 seconds.
# Allow to dry completely.
# Reassemble and test.

✅ Use this if drift is mild or intermittent.
----

==== Repair Option 2: Joystick Module Replacement (Permanent Fix) ====

# Fully disassemble the controller.
# Remove battery and internal shields.
# Expose the joystick module PCB.
# Desolder the joystick module:
#* Add low melt solder to joystick solder points (See Fig. 3)
#* Heat evenly
#* Avoid lifting pads
# Clean solder pads thoroughly.
# Install a new joystick module (OEM or Hall-effect upgrade).
# Solder all anchor and signal pins securely.
# Inspect joints under magnification.
# Reassemble controller.
# Test analog stick response.

✅ This is the recommended long-term fix for stick drift.